ifa/issues/146 E -- the CARTESIAN_PRODUCT splitter (PYC_CPA) was removed 2026-09-08 as arbitrary splitting: it fanned a contour into one per single CreationSet whenever a positional formal's type held 2..N CreationSets, asking for no demand at all (zero references to violation, irrepresentable, dispatch or unresolved in the whole function). A union's EXISTENCE is a fact about the program, not a demand. On THIS fixture it was nevertheless doing real work -- without it `self.aas`'s elements union A and B, so `.ay()` on a B draws `illegal call argument type expression illegal: B`, which is the extra line this test now emits. Note the call resolution is BETTER without it (direct=69 dynamic=0, against CPA's 68/1), so the trade is real but not one-sided. The .check above records the state with no warning, which is what the replacement must reach: demand (an unresolved dispatch or an irrepresentable union) plus dispatch-aware filtering of the RECEIVER, which in single-dispatch OOP is the position that determines dispatch. That fires only where resolution is blocked and acts on the one position that decides it, so it should subsume this fixture and flip this test to PASS.
